#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133500 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ea335d6-6ee6-514f-acd4-deb39d50cf81" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Components in Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "7aec717f-6f52-590d-9cd0-47c34b587e1c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5551" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ k \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$ are orthogonal vectors, find the value of $k$." :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{v}$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot v &= u_{1} \\cdot v_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot v_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot v_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot v_{4} \\\\\n&= 5 \\cdot (-4) + (-3) \\cdot 6 + k \\cdot (-6) + (-2) \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&=-20 - 18 - 6k - 16 \\\\\n&=-6k - 54\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the last line to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-6k - 54 &= 0 \\\\\n- 6k &= 54 \\\\\nk &= -9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133501 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc757fa2-12ce-5a1c-a524-8eb256842079" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Dot Products Using Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "ce2ff5a8-84bb-5d2b-8078-623203f1a3b5" :question/math-academy-id "e-5552" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u} \\!\\perp\\! \\mathbf{w}$. Find $(\\mathbf{u}+\\mathbf{v})\\cdot \\mathbf{w} + \\mathbf{u}\\cdot(\\mathbf{v}+ \\mathbf{w})$." :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{u}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{w}=0\n$$\n\n. Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(u + v) \\cdot w + u \\cdot (v + w) &= u \\cdot w + v \\cdot w + u \\cdot v + u \\cdot w \\\\\n&= 0 + v \\cdot w + u \\cdot v + 0 \\\\\n&= v \\cdot w + u \\cdot v \\\\\n&= (2 \\cdot (-1) + (-3) \\cdot 3 + 4 \\cdot 1) \\\\\n&= + ((-1) \\cdot 2 + (-2) \\cdot (-3) + 5 \\cdot 4) \\\\\n&= (-2 - 9 + 4) + (-2 + 6 + 20) \\\\\n&=-7 + 24 \\\\\n&= 17\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e02a242-6ef9-574a-be2a-2b68b35d761c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Components of a Vector Orthogonal to Two Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "8b0122e7-3500-50cf-8505-22970428dac6" :question/math-academy-id "e-5553" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ a \\\\ b \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$. What is the value of $a+b$?" :question/worked-solution "Given that $\\mathbf{u}$ is orthogonal to $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$, we have\n\n$$\n{u \\cdot v = 0; u \\cdot w = 0\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{v}=0\n$$\n\n. Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot v &= 0 \\\\\n- 8 \\cdot 6 + a \\cdot (-15) + b \\cdot 9 + (-10) \\cdot (-12) &= 0 \\\\\n- 48 - 15a + 9b + 120 &= 0 \\\\\n- 15a + 9b &= -72 \\\\\n- 5a + 3b &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}\\cdot\\mathbf{w}=0\n$$\n\n, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot w &= 0 \\\\\n- 8 \\cdot 4 + a \\cdot 2 + b \\cdot (-5) + (-10) \\cdot (-3) &= 0 \\\\\n- 32 + 2a - 5b + 30 &= 0 \\\\\n2a - 5b &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n{-5a + 3b =-24; 2a - 5b = 2\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and the second equation by $5$, we get\n\n$$\n{-10a + 6b =-48; 10a - 25b = 10\n$$\n\nNow, adding the above equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n-19b = -38 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad b = 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b = 2$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a - 5(2) &= 2 \\\\\n2a - 10 &= 2 \\\\\n2a &= 12 \\\\\na &= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na+b = 6 + 2 = 8\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133553 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ce8958e6-c578-572f-8b34-5513b6f64a51" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "31abdef6-68e0-5c10-b03d-9d835ea6c681" :question/math-academy-id "e-5909" :question/problem "Given the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, which of the following vectors are orthogonal to $\\mathbf{u}$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "We compute the dot product between $\\mathbf{u}$ and each of the listed vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot v &= u_{1} \\cdot v_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot v_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot v_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot v_{4} \\\\\n&= (-5) \\cdot 1 + (-3) \\cdot (-3) + 2 \\cdot (-4) + 0 \\cdot 9 \\\\\n&=-5 + 9 - 8 + 0 \\\\\n&=-4.\\cdot\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot w &= u_{1} \\cdot w_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot w_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot w_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot w_{4} \\\\\n&= (-5) \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot 2 + 2 \\cdot 8 + 0 \\cdot 3 \\\\\n&=-10 - 6 + 16 + 0 \\\\\n&= 0.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot x &= u_{1} \\cdot x_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot x_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot x_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot x_{4} \\\\\n&= (-5) \\cdot 2 + (-3) \\cdot (-4) + 2 \\cdot (-8) + 0 \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&=-10 + 12 - 16 + 0 \\\\\n&=-14.\\cdot\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, the correct answer is $\\mathbf{w}$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134134 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc757fa2-12ce-5a1c-a524-8eb256842079" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Dot Products Using Orthogonal Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82672cb0-6564-54ce-8694-7fca64c06cc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131247} {:answer/id #uuid "85402023-1bba-59b8-aa36-24a9c349fe90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131248} {:answer/id #uuid "cfa7f4b4-a8ab-5ccf-bf74-146546134f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131249} {:answer/id #uuid "38bbe9ae-51ac-52c9-b93b-b8ca5d1c3cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131250} {:answer/id #uuid "63db46b9-15e9-5e25-9188-bb63792946c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63db46b9-15e9-5e25-9188-bb63792946c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131251} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2aa07e2-e28d-5d3e-9c1b-59ec45da4625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131246}] :question/id #uuid "224c287d-59c6-53ff-b3a7-effa4f74d7b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-39333" :question/problem "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $w = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $u⊥v$. Find $(v + w) \\cdot u + v \\cdot (u + w)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134136 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e02a242-6ef9-574a-be2a-2b68b35d761c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Components of a Vector Orthogonal to Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3f32bf3-db88-55c8-9663-26cb47c58ab7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131259} {:answer/id #uuid "d483e405-2656-52f7-a66d-b20e6ec09df0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131260} {:answer/id #uuid "e506fa0b-5e26-5221-9203-6fa72ce9910c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131261} {:answer/id #uuid "ecdff0db-cb85-5541-944a-9009548a6fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131262} {:answer/id #uuid "3d1be6ce-246c-5c12-9645-30e2c7f159f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e506fa0b-5e26-5221-9203-6fa72ce9910c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131261} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bf56cc2-81bf-5fc5-8656-544c880ff619" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131258}] :question/id #uuid "c212d94f-4084-5eee-99e8-30c7436e1711" :question/math-academy-id "q-39337" :question/problem "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 3 \\\\ b \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$, and $w = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w$. What is the value of $a + b$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134177 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e02a242-6ef9-574a-be2a-2b68b35d761c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Components of a Vector Orthogonal to Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd23190-21f8-5764-a64a-ae8b56cf2afc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131505} {:answer/id #uuid "915bd9ea-5ae9-5bf4-a1b4-3fb7163a34b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131506} {:answer/id #uuid "9da95282-6a5c-5b2a-a1b4-2c8bab286e3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131507} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9db635-aac2-5fdd-b710-5b2cda253e3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{47}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131508} {:answer/id #uuid "2643d333-480b-581a-82f7-c8d1f9d1fcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2643d333-480b-581a-82f7-c8d1f9d1fcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131509} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d8c2ce6-d4cd-5692-b876-d2489eaee463" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186131504}] :question/id #uuid "69f9e8f7-7103-5d3a-9398-65c91081214b" :question/math-academy-id "q-40024" :question/problem "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ a \\\\ b \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}, v = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$, and $w = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$ be vectors such that $u⊥v$ and $u⊥w$. What is the value of $a + b$?"}]}
